---
import BaseLayout from "../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/layout/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/layout/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Much Weight Can You Lose on Wegovy? | GLP Index"
  description="The STEP 1 trial answer: people on Wegovy lost an average of 14.9% of body weight over 68 weeks. Here is what that means at different starting weights, and how real results distribute."
  ogImage="/og-wegovy-weight-loss.png"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "How Much Weight Can You Lose on Wegovy?",
      "description": "Clinical trial data from STEP 1 on average weight loss with semaglutide 2.4mg over 68 weeks.",
      "url": "https://glpdash.com/guides/wegovy-weight-loss-results/",
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "GLP Index",
        "url": "https://glpdash.com"
      },
      "dateModified": "2026-05-01",
      "about": {
        "@type": "Drug",
        "name": "Wegovy",
        "activeIngredient": "semaglutide 2.4mg"
      }
    }
  </script>

  <Header />

  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="crumbs">
        <a href="/">GLP Index</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <a href="/guides/">Guides</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span class="now">Wegovy weight loss</span>
      </div>
      <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 20px">Clinical data · Wegovy (semaglutide 2.4mg)</div>
      <h1 class="serif" style="font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(34px,4.5vw,56px);max-width:20ch">
        How much weight can you lose on <em>Wegovy?</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="deck" style="margin-top:18px;max-width:56ch">
        The STEP 1 trial ran for 68 weeks and followed nearly 2,000 people. Here is what it found, broken down by starting weight and where you might realistically land.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="guide-layout">

      <aside class="toc">
        <h4>On this page</h4>
        <a href="#the-number">The trial number</a>
        <a href="#distribution">How results distribute</a>
        <a href="#by-weight">By starting weight</a>
        <a href="#why-it-varies">Why results vary</a>
        <a href="#vs-others">vs. other drugs</a>
        <a href="#calculator">Use the calculator</a>
      </aside>

      <article class="prose guide-body">

        <div class="fact-card" id="the-number">
          <div class="fc-top">
            <span class="fc-label">STEP 1 · Wilding et al. · N Engl J Med 2021</span>
            <a class="cite" href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/10.1056/NEJMoa2032183" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Full paper ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="fc-stat">
            <div class="fc-big serif">14.9%</div>
            <div class="fc-desc">Average body weight lost on Wegovy (semaglutide 2.4mg) over 68 weeks, versus 2.4% on placebo. Both groups followed a reduced-calorie diet and exercise program.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="fc-meta">
            <span>1,961 participants</span>
            <span>68 weeks</span>
            <span>No type 2 diabetes</span>
            <span>BMI ≥ 30, or ≥ 27 with comorbidity</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>
          That is the honest starting point. Not a range. Not "results may vary" without context. The trial enrolled adults with obesity, ran for about 16 months, and measured actual weight change.
        </p>
        <p>
          The average was 14.9% on semaglutide versus 2.4% on placebo. People on Wegovy lost roughly six times more weight than those on an identical program without the drug.
        </p>

        <h2 id="distribution">How results actually distribute</h2>
        <p>
          The 14.9% is the mean. The distribution matters more, because it tells you the realistic range of where people land.
        </p>

        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Weight loss threshold</th>
              <th>Wegovy</th>
              <th>Placebo</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>5% or more</td>
              <td class="num highlight">86%</td>
              <td class="num muted">32%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>10% or more</td>
              <td class="num highlight">69%</td>
              <td class="num muted">12%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>15% or more</td>
              <td class="num highlight">50%</td>
              <td class="num muted">5%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>20% or more</td>
              <td class="num highlight">32%</td>
              <td class="num muted">2%</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>
          Half of everyone who took Wegovy in the trial lost 15% or more. About one in three lost 20% or more. On the low end, roughly 14% lost less than 5%. That group exists, and any honest summary has to include them.
        </p>

        <h2 id="by-weight">What it looks like at your starting weight</h2>
        <p>
          Percentages are consistent but pounds depend on where you start. Here is how 14.9% and the surrounding range translate to actual numbers.
        </p>

        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Starting weight</th>
              <th>5% loss</th>
              <th>10% loss</th>
              <th>15% (avg)</th>
              <th>20% loss</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>180 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">9 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">18 lbs</td>
              <td class="num highlight">27 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">36 lbs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>200 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">10 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">20 lbs</td>
              <td class="num highlight">30 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">40 lbs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>220 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">11 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">22 lbs</td>
              <td class="num highlight">33 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">44 lbs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>250 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">13 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">25 lbs</td>
              <td class="num highlight">37 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">50 lbs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>300 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">15 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">30 lbs</td>
              <td class="num highlight">45 lbs</td>
              <td class="num">60 lbs</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>
          The 15% column is the trial average. The 5% and 20% columns show the range most people fall within based on the responder data above.
        </p>

        <h2 id="why-it-varies">Why your result will differ from the average</h2>
        <p>
          Clinical trials are controlled. Real life is not. A few things that move the needle:
        </p>

        <div class="factor-list">
          <div class="factor">
            <div class="factor-label">Adherence</div>
            <p>The trial measured weekly injections with close monitoring for 68 weeks. Missed doses and early stops reduce total weight loss. The average assumes you finish the course.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="factor">
            <div class="factor-label">Diet and activity</div>
            <p>All participants followed a structured diet and exercise program alongside the medication. The 14.9% number reflects that combination. The drug alone, without lifestyle changes, typically shows lower results.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="factor">
            <div class="factor-label">Individual response</div>
            <p>GLP-1 response varies between people. Some are high responders who lose significantly more than average. Others see minimal effect even at full dose. This is not well predicted in advance.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="factor">
            <div class="factor-label">Time frame</div>
            <p>14.9% is at 68 weeks. Some people plateau before that. Others are still losing at week 68. The week-by-week curve matters more than the endpoint if you are trying to set expectations early on.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="vs-others">How Wegovy compares to the other drugs</h2>
        <p>
          Standard Wegovy is not the highest-performing option in published trials.
        </p>

        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Drug</th>
              <th>Active ingredient</th>
              <th>Trial</th>
              <th>Avg loss</th>
              <th>Duration</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Wegovy HD</td>
              <td class="muted">semaglutide 7.2mg</td>
              <td class="muted">STEP UP (2025)</td>
              <td class="num highlight">20.7%</td>
              <td class="num">72 wks</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Zepbound / Mounjaro</td>
              <td class="muted">tirzepatide</td>
              <td class="muted">SURMOUNT-1</td>
              <td class="num highlight">20.9%</td>
              <td class="num">72 wks</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="active-row">
              <td><strong>Wegovy</strong></td>
              <td class="muted">semaglutide 2.4mg</td>
              <td class="muted">STEP 1</td>
              <td class="num highlight">14.9%</td>
              <td class="num">68 wks</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Ozempic</td>
              <td class="muted">semaglutide 1mg</td>
              <td class="muted">STEP 2</td>
              <td class="num">8.7%</td>
              <td class="num">68 wks</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>
          Ozempic is primarily a diabetes medication, so the STEP 2 population is different and not a direct comparison. Wegovy HD and the tirzepatide drugs (Mounjaro/Zepbound) show higher averages in their respective trials. The mechanisms differ, which is why tirzepatide can produce different outcomes than semaglutide at any dose.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you and your doctor are weighing options and maximum weight loss is the goal, those trials are worth reviewing. The comparison calculator on this site lays out the cost side of that decision.
        </p>

        <div class="cta-box" id="calculator">
          <div class="cta-inner">
            <div>
              <p class="cta-title serif">Project your own timeline</p>
              <p class="cta-sub">Enter your weight and drug. The calculator maps your week-by-week projection against the actual trial curve, with an optional goal weight to see when you might reach it.</p>
            </div>
            <a class="btn btn-p" href="/weight-loss-timeline/">
              Open the calculator <span class="arr">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="source-footer">
          <p class="source-label mono">Primary source</p>
          <p>Wilding JPH, et al. Once-Weekly Semaglutide in Adults with Overweight or Obesity. <em>N Engl J Med.</em> 2021;384(11):989-1002. <a href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/10.1056/NEJMoa2032183" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">doi:10.1056/NEJMoa2032183 ↗</a></p>
        </div>

      </article>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding: 56px 0 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
  }

  .guide-layout {
    padding: 64px 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 64px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* TOC */
  .toc {
    position: sticky;
    top: 88px;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .toc h4 {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6B655C;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .toc a {
    display: block;
    padding: 6px 0 6px 14px;
    color: #3A352E;
    border-left: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
    margin-left: -15px;
    transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .toc a:hover { color: #3F5D52; border-left-color: #3F5D52; }

  /* Article body */
  .guide-body { max-width: 680px; }

  /* Fact card */
  .fact-card {
    background: #E8EDE9;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #3F5D52 25%, #E0DAD0);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .fc-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .fc-label {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #3F5D52;
  }

  .fc-stat {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .fc-big {
    font-size: 52px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: #1A1815;
    line-height: 1;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .fc-desc {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #3A352E;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .fc-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px 20px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #3F5D52 20%, #E0DAD0);
  }

  .fc-meta span {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: #3F5D52;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* Tables */
  .data-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 24px 0 28px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .data-table thead th {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6B655C;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
  }

  .data-table tbody tr {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #EDE7DC;
  }

  .data-table tbody tr:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .data-table tbody td {
    padding: 12px 12px;
    color: #3A352E;
  }

  .data-table tbody tr.active-row td {
    background: #F3F7F4;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .data-table td.num {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #1A1815;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .data-table td.highlight {
    color: #3F5D52;
  }

  .data-table td.muted {
    color: #6B655C;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  /* Factor list */
  .factor-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 24px 0 28px;
  }

  .factor {
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #EDE7DC;
  }

  .factor:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .factor-label {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #3F5D52;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .factor p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #3A352E;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* CTA box */
  .cta-box {
    background: #1A1815;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 28px 32px;
    margin: 48px 0 40px;
  }

  .cta-inner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .cta-title {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #FBFAF7;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .cta-sub {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #9D968C;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 44ch;
  }

  /* Source footer */
  .source-footer {
    padding-top: 32px;
    border-top: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
  }

  .source-label {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6B655C;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .source-footer p {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #6B655C;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .source-footer a {
    color: #3F5D52;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #3F5D52 30%, transparent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .guide-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }
    .toc { position: static; }
    .fc-stat { flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
    .cta-inner { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
  }

  /* Fix .prose a specificity overriding button colors inside article */
  .cta-box a.btn-p {
    color: #FBFAF7;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .cta-box a.btn-p:hover {
    color: #FBFAF7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .data-table {
      display: block;
      overflow-x: auto;
      -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .data-table thead th, .data-table tbody td { padding: 10px 8px; }
    .fc-big { font-size: 40px; }
    .cta-box { padding: 24px 20px; }
    .page-head { padding: 40px 0 32px; }
  }
</style>
